    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0024" n="14" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg14"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24 FLC/2–1348</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to
                        the Chinese Embassy</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide-Mémoire</hi></p>
                <p>Reference is made to negotiations presently going on between representatives in
                    Washington of the Chinese Government and the Field Commissioner for Military
                    Programs, Office of the Foreign Liquidation Commissioner, for the purchase of
                    combat aircraft under the 8⅓ Group Program.</p>
                <p>It is learned that spare parts for P–51 aircraft are in critical shortage.
                    Manufacturers have discontinued production and when present stocks are exhausted
                    there will be no more procurable.</p>
                <p>It is therefore suggested that if the Chinese Government plans to purchase P–51
                    aircraft under the 8⅓ Group Program it would be well advised were it to take
                    advantage of present limited availabilities to purchase an adequate amount of
                    the spare parts in question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-02-11">February 11, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
